<%# locals: (item:, tag_menu_event: nil) %>

<%#
  Adapter between the ledger item view and the tag store. The item view delegates
  the whole "add tag" affordance here; the coupling to the backing HCB code and
  event lives in this partial so a future migration only touches it.

  Only the trigger is per row; `ledgers/_tag_menu` holds the options. A row whose
  HCB code doesn't belong to `tag_menu_event` gets no trigger, because the menu
  it would open holds another organization's tags.

  That membership check is also what stands in for `HcbCodePolicy#toggle_tag?`
  here: `tag_menu_event` is only set for a member of that event, so a code
  carrying it already satisfies the policy. Calling the policy as well would
  re-run `HcbCode#events` — which doesn't memoize — for every row.
%>
<% hcb_code = item.hcb_code %>
<% if tag_menu_event.present? && hcb_code.present? && hcb_code.events.include?(tag_menu_event) %>
  <button
    type="button"
    class="list-badge add-tag-badge !mx-0 menu__toggle menu__toggle--arrowless"
    style="margin-left: 0.5rem;"
    data-hcb-code="<%= hcb_code.hashid %>"
    data-action="ledger-tag-menu#toggle">+ Add tag</button>
<% end %>
